(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the electrical architecture of an Electric Vehicle \(EV\) powertrain, explaining the function of each constituent block.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Electric Vehicle \(EV\) Powertrain Architecture:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. High-Voltage Traction Battery Pack:) Tj
T*
(   Constructed from series-parallel configurations of lithium-ion cells \(typically 400V or 800V DC) Tj
T*
(   nominal bus\). Serves as the prime energy reservoir.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Battery Management System \(BMS\):) Tj
T*
(   A safety-critical embedded electronic unit that measures individual cell voltages, module) Tj
T*
(   temperatures, and pack current. Executes State-of-Charge \(SoC\) estimation, State-of-Health) Tj
T*
(   \(SoH\) diagnostics, thermal management, passive/active cell balancing, and high-voltage) Tj
T*
(   contactor disconnect protection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. High-Voltage Traction Inverter:) Tj
T*
(   A 3-phase bidirectional DC-AC converter utilizing silicon carbide \(SiC\) MOSFETs or IGBTs. It) Tj
T*
(   synthesizes variable-frequency, variable-voltage AC power using Space Vector Pulse Width) Tj
T*
(   Modulation \(SVPWM\) governed by Field-Oriented Control \(FOC\) algorithms to drive the electric) Tj
T*
(   motor with high torque precision.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Electric Traction Motor:) Tj
T*
(   Typically an Interior Permanent Magnet Synchronous Motor \(IPMSM\) or 3-phase Squirrel-Cage) Tj
T*
(   Induction Motor, converting electrical energy into mechanical propulsion with efficiencies) Tj
T*
ET

