(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the Field-Oriented Control \(FOC\) mathematical framework for Permanent Magnet Synchronous Motors \(PMSMs\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Field-Oriented Control \(FOC\) Mathematical Formulation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   FOC decouples electromagnetic torque generation from rotor magnetic flux generation in AC) Tj
T*
(   synchronous machines, establishing control dynamics analogous to a separately excited DC motor.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Clarke Transformation \(Stationary 3-Phase $abc$ to Stationary 2-Phase $\\alpha\\beta$\):) Tj
T*
(   $$\\begin{bmatrix} i_\\alpha \\\\ i_\\beta \\end{bmatrix} = \\frac{2}{3} \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1/2 &) Tj
T*
(   -1/2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}/2 & -\\sqrt{3}/2 \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} i_a \\\\ i_b \\\\ i_c) Tj
T*
(   \\end{bmatrix}$$) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Park Transformation \(Stationary $\\alpha\\beta$ to Synchronously Rotating $dq$ Reference) Tj
T*
(   Frame\):) Tj
T*
(   $$\\begin{bmatrix} i_d \\\\ i_q \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} \\cos\\theta_e & \\sin\\theta_e \\\\) Tj
T*
(   -\\sin\\theta_e & \\cos\\theta_e \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} i_\\alpha \\\\ i_\\beta \\end{bmatrix}$$) Tj
T*
(   where $\\theta_e$ is the instantaneous rotor electrical angle measured by an optical rotary) Tj
T*
(   encoder or resolver.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Decoupled Torque and Flux Control Equations:) Tj
T*
(   For a non-salient PMSM \($L_d = L_q = L_s$\):) Tj
T*
(   $$T_e = \\frac{3}{2} P \\lambda_{pm} i_q$$) Tj
T*
(   - The direct-axis current $i_d$ controls rotor flux: setting $i_d^* = 0$ achieves maximum) Tj
T*
(   torque per ampere \(MTPA\), while negative $i_d^* < 0$ achieves flux weakening for high-speed) Tj
T*
(   operation above base speed.) Tj
T*
(   - The quadrature-axis current $i_q$ controls developed torque linearly.) Tj
T*
(   4. Current Regulation: Two independent PI controllers regulate $i_d$ and $i_q$, generating) Tj
T*
(   reference voltages $v_d^*$ and $v_q^*$, which are transformed back via Inverse Park and fed to) Tj
T*
(   a Space Vector PWM modulator.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
