BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the principles, operation, and grid integration challenges of Utility-Scale Solar Photovoltaic Power Plants.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Utility-Scale Solar Photovoltaic Systems:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Plant Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   Consists of thousands of photovoltaic modules mounted on single-axis solar trackers organized) Tj
T*
(   into series strings and parallel arrays connected to DC combiner boxes. DC power is inverted to) Tj
T*
(   medium-voltage AC \(typically 33 kV\) by central or string inverters, and then stepped up to grid) Tj
T*
(   voltage \(132 kV / 220 kV / 400 kV\) via station step-up transformers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Maximum Power Point Tracking \(MPPT\):) Tj
T*
(   Inverters continuously track solar array I-V characteristics to operate at $V_{mpp}$ under) Tj
T*
(   variable solar irradiance \($G$\) and ambient module temperatures \($T$\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Grid Interconnection Challenges:) Tj
T*
(   - Intermittency and Weather Dependence: Cloud transients produce severe power ramp rates \($>) Tj
T*
(   50\\text{ MW/min}$\), stressing grid frequency regulation.) Tj
T*
(   - Harmonics and Power Quality: Switching harmonics from high-power PWM inverters must comply) Tj
T*
(   strictly with IEEE 519 limits at the Point of Common Coupling \(PCC\).) Tj
T*
(   - Low-Voltage Ride-Through \(LVRT\): Grid codes require solar plants to stay connected during) Tj
T*
(   grid voltage dips and inject reactive current to support voltage recovery.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
