T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the Green Hydrogen economy: Electrolyzer technologies \(Alkaline, PEM, Solid Oxide\) and power electronic converter requirements.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Green Hydrogen Generation via Water Electrolysis:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Hydrogen Production Technologies:) Tj
T*
(   - Alkaline Electrolysis \(AEL\): Uses liquid potassium hydroxide \($KOH$\) electrolyte with nickel) Tj
T*
(   catalysts. Mature, low capital cost, operating at $60-90^\\circ\\text{C}$ with specific energy) Tj
T*
(   consumption $\\approx 50-55 \\text{ kWh/kg } H_2$.) Tj
T*
(   - Proton Exchange Membrane \(PEM\) Electrolysis: Uses a solid polymer electrolyte and precious) Tj
T*
(   metal catalysts \(platinum, iridium\). Operates at higher current densities and responds within) Tj
T*
(   milliseconds to fluctuating renewable solar/wind power.) Tj
T*
(   - Solid Oxide Electrolysis Cells \(SOEC\): Operates at high temperatures) Tj
T*
(   \($700-850^\\circ\\text{C}$\) utilizing steam, achieving thermal-electrical efficiencies) Tj
T*
(   approaching 90%.) Tj
T*
ET

