(   2. Power Electronic Converter Requirements:) Tj
T*
(   Electrolyzers require massive direct current \(thousands of Amperes DC\) at relatively low) Tj
T*
(   voltages \($100-500\\text{ V}$\). Power converters must provide:) Tj
T*
(   - Extremely low current ripple \(< 2%\) to prevent catalyst degradation and preserve membrane) Tj
T*
(   life.) Tj
T*
(   - Multi-Pulse Thyristor Rectifiers \(12-pulse/24-pulse\) with interphase reactors or Active Front) Tj
T*
(   End \(AFE\) PWM rectifiers maintaining high input power factor \($> 0.98$\) and compliance with) Tj
T*
(   grid harmonic standards.) Tj
