(>> Solution to Question 8:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the principles of Battery Management Systems \(BMS\): State of Charge \(SoC\), State of Health \(SoH\), and cell balancing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Battery Management System \(BMS\) Engineering:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. State of Charge \(SoC\) Estimation:) Tj
T*
(   - Coulomb Counting Method: Integrates battery current over time: $\\text{SoC}\(t\) =) Tj
T*
(   \\text{SoC}\(t_0\) - \\frac{1}{C_n} \\int_0^t I\(\\tau\) d\\tau$. Susceptible to accumulated current) Tj
T*
(   sensor drift.) Tj
T*
(   - Extended Kalman Filter \(EKF\): Combines Coulomb counting with equivalent circuit models) Tj
T*
(   \(Thevenin dual-polarization RC networks\) and Open Circuit Voltage \(OCV\) lookups to compute) Tj
T*
(   optimal, drift-free SoC estimates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. State of Health \(SoH\) Diagnostics:) Tj
T*
(   Evaluates capacity loss and internal resistance growth \($R_{int}$\) over charge-discharge aging) Tj
T*
(   cycles: $\\text{SoH} = \\frac{C_{actual}}{C_{nominal}} \\times 100\\%$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Cell Balancing Mechanisms:) Tj
T*
(   - Passive Balancing: Switched bleed resistors dissipate energy as heat from cells with higher) Tj
T*
(   voltage until all cells match.) Tj
T*
ET

