(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the architecture and communication protocol of CANbus in automotive and industrial control systems.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Controller Area Network \(CANbus\) Architecture:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Layer: Balanced differential two-wire bus \(CAN_H and CAN_L\) terminated at both) Tj
T*
(   cable ends with $120\\,\\Omega$ resistors. Operates with dominant \(logic 0, differential voltage) Tj
T*
(   $\\approx 2\\text{ V}$\) and recessive \(logic 1, differential voltage $\\approx 0\\text{ V}$\)) Tj
T*
(   states.) Tj
T*
(   2. Non-Destructive Bitwise Arbitration: When multiple nodes transmit simultaneously, the node) Tj
T*
(   transmitting the lowest numerical Identifier \(highest priority\) wins the bus without data) Tj
T*
(   corruption.) Tj
T*
(   3. Error Detection & Confinement: Employs CRC-15 checksums, bit stuffing, frame checks, and) Tj
T*
(   automatic node isolation \(Bus Off state\) upon persistent transmit/receive errors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
