(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the working and control of Active Power Factor Correction \(PFC\) circuits in modern power supplies.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Active Power Factor Correction \(PFC\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Uncorrected diode bridge rectifiers draw narrow, high-amplitude current pulses at AC voltage) Tj
T*
(   peaks, causing poor power factor \($0.6-0.7$\) and high Total Harmonic Distortion \(THD\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Boost PFC Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   A boost converter topology is inserted between the diode rectifier and DC output capacitor. An) Tj
T*
(   inner high-speed current control loop forces the input inductor current to track a rectified) Tj
T*
(   sinusoidal reference in phase with input AC voltage, achieving unity power factor \($> 0.99$\)) Tj
T*
(   and compliance with IEC 61000-3-2 standards.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
