(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the working principles of Dual Active Bridge \(DAB\) converters in bidirectional power applications.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Dual Active Bridge \(DAB\) DC-DC Converter:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Topology: Consists of two full-bridge active converter bridges separated by a high-frequency) Tj
T*
(   isolation transformer and series leakage inductor.) Tj
T*
(   2. Phase-Shift Modulation: Both bridges generate high-frequency square wave voltages across the) Tj
T*
(   transformer. Power flow direction and magnitude are controlled strictly by adjusting the) Tj
T*
(   phase-shift angle $\\phi$ between primary and secondary AC square waves:) Tj
T*
(   $$P = \\frac{V_1 V_2}{2 \\pi f_s L} \\phi \\left\( 1 - \\frac{|\\phi|}{\\pi} \\right\)$$) Tj
T*
(   Provides natural Zero Voltage Switching \(ZVS\) across broad load ranges.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
