T*
(   Revenue Instrument Transformers:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Ratio and Phase Angle Errors: In practical transformers, magnetizing current \($I_0$\) and) Tj
T*
(   winding impedances create ratio error and phase displacement between primary and secondary) Tj
T*
(   phasors.) Tj
T*
(   2. Accuracy Classes: Revenue metering demands high precision \(Class 0.2S or 0.5S under IEC) Tj
T*
(   61869-2\). The 'S' designation guarantees accuracy maintained across wide dynamic current ranges) Tj
T*
(   \(from 1% to 120% of rated current\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Burden: The secondary connected impedance \(meters, wiring\) must not exceed the rated burden) Tj
T*
(   \(VA\) to prevent saturation and severe metering errors.) Tj
